      "title": "Read me",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "MiniMax H3 S3 + corrector\n\nCFG 1. S3 is guidance-distilled, so it runs one forward per step. The negative prompt is ignored at CFG 1.\n\nShift 12 for video and 3 for audio, Euler, simple schedule.\n\nApply H3 Corrector runs on every step by default.\n  start_step / end_step: 0-based and inclusive; -1 = through the last step.\n  Example: 0 / 4 on 20 steps corrects only the first 5.\n  strength 0 turns it off.\n  budget_fraction 0.5 and velocity_floor 0.001 are what the S3 corrector was trained with.\n\nThe corrector stays fp32 (about 8 GB VRAM), because bf16 weights change its output.\n\nlength snaps to 17k+5 frames at 24 fps: 56 is about 2 s, 124 about 5 s.\n\nThe S3 pipeline prompts with structured JSON captions (written by its prompt enhancer), like the one in the positive prompt.\n\nSpeed on an RTX 3090 Ti (needs PyTorch cu130 for the W4A8 kernels):\n  672x384, 124 frames: 5.7 s/step\n  1344x736, 56 frames: 11.5 s/step"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "MiniMax H3 S3 + corrector\n\nCFG 1. S3 is guidance-distilled, so it runs one forward per step. The negative prompt is ignored at CFG 1.\n\nShift 12 for video and 3 for audio, Euler, simple schedule.\n\nApply H3 Corrector runs on every step by default.\n  start_step / end_step: 0-based and inclusive; -1 = through the last step.\n  Example: 0 / 4 on 20 steps corrects only the first 5.\n  strength 0 turns it off.\n  budget_fraction 0.5 and velocity_floor 0.001 are what the S3 corrector was trained with.\n\nThe corrector stays fp32 (about 8 GB VRAM), because bf16 weights change its output.\n\nlength snaps to 17k+5 frames at 24 fps: 56 is about 2 s, 124 about 5 s.\n\nThe S3 pipeline prompts with structured JSON captions (written by its prompt enhancer), like the one in the positive prompt.\n\nSpeed on an RTX 3090 Ti (needs PyTorch cu130 for the W4A8 kernels):\n  672x384, 124 frames: 5.7 s/step\n  1344x736, 56 frames: 11.5 s/step"
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
